# Conditional adaptive lifetime composition — design only

This proposes the next integration boundary for the implemented mathematical
request circuits. It is not an implemented lifetime driver, a new primitive
assumption, a family-wide maximum, or a complete B6.1 resource certificate.
No frozen argument, ledger, source, candidate status or production gate changes.

## 1. Explicit finite experiment

Fix M=2^20, an honest typed-request cap T, external combined-oracle call cap Q,
stored-message capacity W=215150 bytes, response width v=2112 bits, and length
width b. Fix each external full-message capacity C_j with W<=C_j<2^b; the
current actual L0 factory additionally requires C_j>=6882996. Query count
alone gives no length bound. Set N=T*(M+2), k=b+8W and d=max(2,N.bit_length()).
The array has N*(1+k+v) bits; allocate d counter bits once, even if T=0 leaves
that counter unused. Current factory bounds require T<=2^64. T here caps ALL
three typed request families, including rejected calls; if the accepted experiment
bounds only valid requests, rejected-call counts need separate explicit caps.

Honest requests are classical and atomic. A trusted typed descriptor selects:
(a) a REG RequestTransition with legal body/context length family;
(b) a VOTE ContentFamily for actual length3..1000, including all invalid content;
(c) a RejectedVoteFamily for a fixed other64-bit actual length, including invalid
vote bytes. The third family does not allocate/read the list or sample coins;
it borrows and preserves its complete typed input. Descriptor authentication,
classical family selection and transport/codec work are explicit driver premises
and separate costs. This proposal gives no coherent request-generation API.
REG retains its97+proof-bit return; the VOTE family union has253+proof bits.
Unifying the two role returns requires a further adapter or typed role interface.

External queries use canonical length/full-message registers, an enable bit and
an arbitrary response target. Every fixed/variable F adapter refers to the same
immutable source-domain-padded function, including exactly ten native H5 bits.
Unknown/empty messages and noncanonical encodings require an agreed fixed total
completion. No new random tails, query validation or base-oracle implementation
are supplied here. The provided F may be correlated with adversary/reference
state; its value/register is unchanged by response-XOR calls.

## 2. Exact conditional event-cost vector

For a realized sequence rho of r<=T typed requests and q<=Q external calls,
let g_i=(X_i,CX_i,CCX_i,F_i) be that selected request family's current resource
vector, instantiated at the SAME N and b. Rejected-size families make no log
access. ContentFamily adds96 output wires and no gates to ContentRequest.
All bounded-content requests, including rejected ones, pay the full generator,
valid-controlled W, return and inverse. Smaller trial caps are test models only.

For N>0 one external L0 event costs exactly:

```
l = (4kN+4N+2, 4kN, N*(4k+6+v)+v+2, 2),
w_L = 2N+k+v+2 clean bits.
```

For N=0 it costs (0,0,v,2) and v clean bits. Each query also uses b+8C_j
query bits, one enable bit and v caller-response bits; these are not scratch.
No second append counter or persistent-log allocation belongs to L0.

The conditional implemented-circuit sum is g_body(rho)=sum_i g_i+q*l.
Its elementary subtotal is X+CX+5*CCX, keeping F queries separate. Concretely,
F_body=6200*n_candidate_generating+5960*n_comparator_generating+2q;
"generating" includes bounded-content rejection, but excludes size-rejected VOTE.
W/E make no F calls. Honest internal reads use the base directly because their
complete messages end in0/1/4/5/8 and the log programs only9/10/11. Do NOT charge
L0 again for these reads or insert the earlier741-read source subtotal into this
circuit count. Compute/unquery and outer generator inverse are already included.

The full experiment needs the separate addition
`g_total=g_body+g_adversary+g_input/coin-preparation+g_selection/routing+g_init`.
A concrete implementation of F would add its actual per-call gate/work costs;
in an oracle model its calls and retained state stay separate resources. No
unit cost for F, variable-length routing, adaptive control or quantum RAM is assumed.
The adversary subtotal excludes the Q lookup invocations already charged; any
extra verifier/diagnostic/final-comparison calls must enter Q or separate terms.
For this trace, each event has a specified cost. An accepted uniform worst-case
certificate still needs bounds over ALL admissible traces/families, or explicit
per-family quotas/envelopes. The four endpoint observations do not supply them.

## 3. Capacity and adaptive joint-state induction

Start with a zero log and c=0. Every generating request appends at most M+2
records, including all M primary writes on exhaustion; auxiliary trials never
write. Bounded-content rejection and size rejection append zero. Therefore before
request i at most(i-1)*(M+2) slots are used and a generating request has capacity.
All disabled scans remain charged. L0 leaves log/counter unchanged and returns
the newest matching active record, preserving arbitrary correlations on disjoint registers (duplicate key bytes
remain permitted). Canonical query and active-record encodings are a premise
on the entire quantum support; a total F completion does not validate them.

Use the clean component identity at each entering history, then compose the
resulting channels/isometries in actual event order. Fresh coins are independent
of the entering history when drawn, not necessarily independent conditional on
the COMPLETED adaptive trace: later requests can reveal earlier outcomes. The
trace labels above are resource bookkeeping, not a change to the sampling law.
No adversary action occurs between a request's G/W/E/G-inverse or between L0's
two base calls. Each component restores its clean work before the next event.
The whole proof must preserve the joint log, F, caller and adversary/reference
state; equality of returned proof distributions alone is insufficient.

## 4. Storage, retained randomness and initial state

For request i let U_i be its typed public bits, R_i its original private coins,
O_i its caller output, H_i its retained derived outputs and S_i its shared work.
Generating R_i=512*M+256*T_open+896*tau+tau*ell+10*g+736*8.
Rejected-size requests have R_i=H_i=0, S_i=519, U_i=3608+1024*n and the row's
common VOTE output O_i. Their borrowed list storage is real input storage even
though none of its bits are read. It is not newly allocated by the rejection map.

One transparent conservative ownership convention retains distinct original
input/coin/return slots for every request and distinct query/response slots for
every external event. These slots are supplied directly, never cloned from an
unknown quantum state. Adversary filling, moving or retaining data in them is
charged in g_adversary or the explicit routing term. If A excludes these interface
slots and B_F denotes the supplied oracle state, the allocated logical space is:

```
B_log + d + A + B_F + D
+ sum_i(U_i+R_i+O_i) + sum_j(b+8C_j+1+v) + E + K,
K >= max({H_i+S_i}_i union {w_L}).
```

D names additional driver/control/history storage. E names coin-purification
or retained environment registers. Empty maxima are0. Clean request history and
L0 scratch share K because each is zero at event boundaries; original coin and
caller-output slots do not belong to that reusable workspace. This is exact for
the stated disjoint allocation, or a bound when budgets exceed used slots. It
is not automatically a preallocated uniform bound: choosing A,D,E,K and interface
slot budgets for all adaptive branches is a remaining obligation. If interfaces
are already included in A, count their union once instead of adding them twice.

In a classical-randomness model, each coin register begins uniformly mixed and
may be discarded after the atomic request; visible joint evolution is the
mixture over the same per-tape maps. Safe disposal/reinitialization and histories
then belong to the classical-environment resource model. They are not a unitary
reset. In a fully retained purification model, keep every R_i register and its
purifier: a canonical preparation uses R_i Hadamards and R_i CNOTs from2R_i zero
bits, with E=sum_i R_i. Those Hadamards/preparation are ADDITIONAL resources absent
from the current X/CX/CCX subtotal. An arbitrary environment implementation may
cost more. Freshness/entropy-source acceptance remains separate from this model.

The log, counter and K work wires must initially be clean; returned targets may
be arbitrary for XOR semantics, or supplied zero to read ordinary result bytes.
Providing/preparing all these states, public inputs, F and the adversary state
requires named initial resources. The logical formula measures none of the native
64 MiB verifier workspace, physical qubits, hardware time or allocation behavior.

